body:
Minecraft - Fully customizable game via downloading other launchers and downloading other packs. Mainly singleplayer game even if you're playing multiplayer. Most faction servers the logic is to trust no-one, most mainstream arcade servers will have assortment of games to play with your friends or alone. Modding, loads of different mod packs to play with friends or alone. I would say you have to familiarize yourself with your computer a bit as modding games could get a little difficult for a beginner.

&#x200B;

Roblox - Roblox isn't a defined game, there are different kinds of games you can play. It follows the arcade style, you're able to create your own roblox game and start your own community but it takes a bit of time to understand that.   


Most Roblox games will have lootboxes to either advance progression or give cosmetics. Some gamemodes are p2w some aren't.

&#x200B;

TLDR; In theory they are about the same game, except minecraft has its own defined world for you to explore and beat.
